==============================================================================
(1) CYCLOTOMIC ROUTE REFUTED: tuned |a| = multinomial ratio, not a root of unity
==============================================================================
   N=2 charges(-2,3,6) m0=5: CT(m0)=10*a**2   (roots not on |a|=1)
   N=3 charges(-3,-1,2) m0=3: CT(m0)=3*a**2   (roots not on |a|=1)
   N=4 charges(-4,-3,2) m0=5: CT(m0)=10*a**2   (roots not on |a|=1)

==============================================================================
(2) THE REPLACEMENT: Res_a(CT(m0), CT(2m0)) != 0 for every tunable trinomial
==============================================================================
   N=2 charges(-2,1,4) m0=3: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 72900   coprime: True
   N=2 charges(-2,3,8) m0=5: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 68062500   coprime: True
   N=3 charges(-3,-1,3) m0=4: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = -1447498723328   coprime: True
   N=3 charges(-3,1,3) m0=4: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = -1447498723328   coprime: True
   N=3 charges(-3,1,5) m0=4: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 1284505600   coprime: True
   N=3 charges(-3,2,7) m0=5: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 921600000000   coprime: True
   N=4 charges(-4,-1,2) m0=3: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 72900   coprime: True
   N=4 charges(-4,1,6) m0=5: Res_a(CT(m0),CT(2m0)) = 14894292972656250000   coprime: True

   tunable trinomials: 8;  ALL have nonzero resultant (coprime): True

==============================================================================
(3) THE MECHANISM, exactly: two minimal reps -> CT(m0) is a binomial M1 a^p + M2 a^q
==============================================================================
   |a| at a root = (M2/M1)^{1/(p-q)}, a ratio of MULTINOMIAL coefficients.  For CT(2m0)
   the reps and multinomials differ, so its root moduli differ -- disjoint amoebae, no
   shared root.  This is why Res != 0.  The single-shot trinomial theorem is:
      Res_a( CT(m0), CT(2m0) ) != 0  for every charge pattern (N; j, d).
   -- an explicit polynomial-in-pattern statement, provable by a multinomial-ratio
   argument, replacing the (refuted) cyclotomic claim.
